        <mxCell id="c150" value="Business / organizational activity" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="737" y="1163" width="500" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c151" value="&lt;b&gt;Why this order&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. The ABS rate master and its Kafka feed (MS2) block everything that shows rates.&lt;br&gt;2. Rates for the website and both call centers go live first (Release 1, MS3): small and low-risk, and the call centers are ready before clients start calling.&lt;br&gt;3. Online applications (Release 2, MS4) follow; the marketing campaign (MS5) starts only after both releases.&lt;br&gt;4. The partner track starts in M1 with the contract and file spec, because the partner builds its import in its own IS." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1300" y="1090" width="1350" height="160" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c152" value="" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#222222;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="65" y="1210" width="18" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
